113 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 63 0 R/T(Previous and current readings are inputs used to calculate consumption. Household number identifies the consumer and category identifies the consumer class. Units, energy charge, fixed charge and total are outputs. The tariff limits and rates remain unchanged during one run, so they are constants. Readings and units are whole numbers. Money is represented in paise to avoid decimal rounding. The bill must never be negative and total must equal energy charge plus fixed charge. If readings are stored as text, converting and comparing d digits takes O\(d\) time and d+1 bytes per string; an integer comparison is O\(1\) and uses sizeof\(int\) bytes.)/E(Previous and current readings are inputs used to calculate consumption. Household number identifies the consumer and category identifies the consumer class. Units, energy charge, fixed charge and total are outputs. The tariff limits and rates remain unchanged during one run, so they are constants. Readings and units are whole numbers. Money is represented in paise to avoid decimal rounding. The bill must never be negative and total must equal energy charge plus fixed charge. If readings are stored as text, converting and comparing d digits takes O\(d\) time and d+1 bytes per string; an integer comparison is O\(1\) and uses sizeof\(int\) bytes.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

