<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 71 0 R/T(Use %d for int, %u for unsigned int, %ld for long, %lld for long long, %f for float in printf, %lf for double in printf, %c for char and %s for a string. In scanf, %f reads float and %lf reads double. A wrong specifier causes undefined behaviour. scanf returns the number of successfully assigned values. For paise, p/100 gives rupees and p%100 gives paise.)/E(Use %d for int, %u for unsigned int, %ld for long, %lld for long long, %f for float in printf, %lf for double in printf, %c for char and %s for a string. In scanf, %f reads float and %lf reads double. A wrong specifier causes undefined behaviour. scanf returns the number of successfully assigned values. For paise, p/100 gives rupees and p%100 gives paise.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[9]>>
