1092 0 obj
<</Title(Use sizeof to measure storage and limits.h/float.h to inspect ranges. unsigned short is commonly 2 bytes and stores 0\20565535. Use int for ordinary numeric IDs, char for a one-character category, unsigned integer types for non-negative readings, and long long for district paise totals. Store money as integer paise, not float rupees, because decimal fractions such as 0.1 are not represented exactly in binary. A 16-bit register wraps modulo 65536. A typical float is 4 bytes and long long is 8 bytes; exact sizes depend on the compiler.)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1022 0 R>>
endobj

