<</Title(The five example bills total Rs 1,487.50. The rollover test returns 256 units. The district-scale example of 800,000 bills at Rs 10,000 each is 800 billion paise, which does not fit a 32-bit int but fits a 64-bit accumulator. A #define tariff requires recompilation after a change. A configuration file takes O\(t\) time and space to read t values at start-up but permits tariff updates without rebuilding the executable.)/Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1101 0 R>>
endobj

1127 0 obj
<</Title(The new system handles interval energy in Wh, timestamps and separate peak/off-peak totals. A 16-bit register cannot hold an illustrative annual energy of 35,040 kWh = 35,040,000 Wh. Use a 64-bit accumulator. The tariff values are read from tariff.cfg rather than compiled as #define values. Peak hours are 18:00 inclusive to 22:00 exclusive. The program assumes each record contains interval Wh, not a cumulative register reading.)/Dest[27 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1103 0 R>>
endobj

