<</Title(The calculated totals are 4,000,000,000; 60,000,000,000; and 800,000,000,000 paise. All exceed a typical signed 32-bit int. They fit in a 64-bit long long. Exact sizeof and limits depend on the system. A double can hold the magnitude, but it may lose single-paise precision at sufficiently large values; long long paise is preferred for exact currency.)/Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1148 0 R>>
endobj

1174 0 obj
<</Title(Use a documented 16-bit meter type only when the hardware register is exactly 16-bit. Use wider unsigned integers for consumption, integer paise for currency, and long long/int64_t for district totals. Centralise tariffs in one header or validated configuration. Include guards protect headers. Use functions for calculations and avoid side-effecting macro arguments. Validate all inputs and check arithmetic bounds.)/Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1151 0 R>>
endobj

