1191 0 obj
<</Title(For 65400 to 120, consumption is 256 units. The energy charge is 56 \327 225 + 100 \327 450 = 57,600 paise; adding the fixed charge gives Rs 626.00. Boundary test bills are 0 units = Rs 50.00, 100 = Rs 50.00, 200 = Rs 275.00 and 350 = Rs 950.00. Five bills at 0, 100, 150, 200 and 350 units total Rs 1,487.50. Invalid letters, negative values and implausible decreases must be rejected. An array-and-loop tariff design takes O\(s\) time for s slabs and uses O\(s\) configuration space; fixed slab statements are O\(1\) and simpler for three fixed slabs.)/Dest[23 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1168 0 R>>
endobj

1192 0 obj
<</Title(An individual bill and a district accumulator need different ranges. This experiment assumes a maximum bill of Rs 10,000, or 1,000,000 paise. At 800,000 bills the total is 800,000,000,000 paise, larger than a typical 32-bit int but within a 64-bit long long. float has about 24 bits of significand precision and double about 53; a large range does not guarantee exact paise. Integer addition and floating addition are O\(1\); typical float is 4 bytes and long long/double are 8 bytes.)/Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1171 0 R>>
endobj

