<</Title(Small integer types are promoted to int before arithmetic. The usual arithmetic conversions choose a common type for mixed expressions. Integer division removes the fractional part. A cast to int cannot preserve a value outside int's range. For decimal charges, use a documented rounding rule such as nearest paise. Widen before multiplication, for example \(long long\)units * rate.)/Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1246 0 R>>
endobj

