1266 0 obj
<</Title(The preprocessor replaces RATE with 225 and inserts standard-header declarations. The assembly file contains processor instructions; the object file contains machine code; the executable is linked. A missing semicolon is a compile-time error, an undefined compute_bill reference is a link-time error, and invalid run-time input is handled by program validation. In a multi-file project, only a changed .c file needs recompilation if its header interface is unchanged; object files require additional disk space.)/Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1251 0 R>>
endobj

1267 0 obj
<</Title(The meter is treated as a 16-bit unsigned register. A lower current reading may indicate rollover or invalid input. This demonstration accepts rollover only when the previous value is at least 60000 and current value is at most 5535. This is an explicit plausibility rule; a production system should use meter protocol information. The bill uses integer paise and progressive slabs.)/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1254 0 R>>
endobj

