<</Title(gcc -E creates preprocessed source with macros expanded and headers included. gcc -S creates assembly. gcc -c creates an object file without linking. Linking combines object files and libraries into an executable. A compile-time error is a source syntax/type error; a link-time error is a missing definition; a run-time error occurs while the executable runs. -Wall -Wextra enable useful warnings.)/Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1264 0 R>>
endobj

